With the fifth beta of <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a>, Apple has expanded the voice customization options for <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> AI.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/ios-27-siri-voice.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1059148" /><br/>
Pace and Expressivity can now be adjusted for more of the available voice options instead of just the two American voices.<br/>
<br/>
There are seven American voice options and four British voices to choose from, all of which can be customized with different Pace and Expressivity settings. Pace changes talking speed, while expressivity changes emphasis.<br/>
<br/>
&zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI voice customization is done on-device, so the feature is limited to newer iPhones. You need an <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-17-pro/">iPhone 17 Pro</a>, &zwnj;iPhone 17 Pro&zwnj; Max, or <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-air/">iPhone Air</a> to use voice customization on an iPhone.<br/>
<br/>
